{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 104, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a weak avg_pool on the direct input-to-output edge with a conv gives large gains on all datasets."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading a skip_connect on the final edge to conv_3x3 yields about +16 to +24 points, much more than edits from other ops."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv where the edge was missing gives a much larger gain than swapping one existing op for another."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a conv_3x3 on the output edge costs far more than removing a weaker op."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a conv_3x3 on the direct edge with pooling is a big loss, unlike replacing skip_connect."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 0 already a skip_connect, skip_connect on edge 2 leaves too little learnable capacity, giving large drops."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a conv_3x3 on the input edge with skip_connect loses capacity and hurts consistently."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding conv_3x3 where the input edge was removed restores a learnable path and gives a large gain."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping skip_connect for pooling on edge 4